cipher-platform (2.0) jammy; urgency=medium

  * K.1.5 Step 2 Sub-step 0 rev8 (2026-05-27): cipher_vllm_kv.py
    _ensure_bridge_init applies max(compute_va_gib, _VA_POOL_HARDCODED
    _FALLBACK_GIB=80) as VA pool floor. Closes pre-existing
    TinyLlama-AWQ slab_create "no VA run of N pages" failure surfaced
    by W.6 sub-A engagement verification. Root cause: per-model
    compute_va_gib() formula systematically underestimates KV pool
    size for quantized workloads (vLLM allocates num_gpu_blocks
    based on gpu_memory_utilization * HBM - weights; when weights
    are small INT4, the saved memory becomes more KV blocks beyond
    the formula's max_batch * per-seq-tokens estimate). For
    TinyLlama-AWQ util=0.3 the formula returned 13 GiB; vLLM
    actually allocated 22+ GiB across 22 layers. Fix is additive:
    cuMemAddressReserve is VA-only (no physical pin), so the
    generous 80 GiB floor has zero physical cost. Memory #16
    backfill discipline; not a substrate rebuild. Customer can
    still override via CIPHER_KV_VA_POOL_GIB.

